This can be achieved using a single HTML file with embedded CSS for simplicity.

Since I cannot provide a physical video file, I will use a placeholder URL (`your-video-url.mp4`). **You must replace this placeholder with the actual URL of your video file.**

### `index.html`

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Explore Zeroh</title>
    <style>
        /* Reset and Global Styling */
        body, html {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            height: 100%; /* Essential for full viewport coverage */
            width: 100%;
            background-color: black;
            overflow: hidden; /* Ensures the page is not scrollable */
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, "Open Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
        }

        /* Video Background Styling */
        .video-background {
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            object-fit: cover; /* Ensures the video covers the entire area without distortion */
            z-index: 0; /* Keeps the video behind the content */
        }

        /* Hero Content Centering */
        .hero-content {
            position: relative; /* Ensures content sits above the video (z-index 1) */
            z-index: 1;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100%;
            text-align: center;
            color: white; /* Default text color */
        }

        /* Text Styling */
        .hero-text {
            font-size: 5em; /* Large size */
            font-weight: 900; /* Bold */
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5); /* Helps text stand out over the video */
        }

        /* Button Styling (Initial State) */
        .waitlist-button {
            padding: 15px 35px;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            font-weight: bold;
            color: white;
            border: 2px solid white;
            background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); /* Transparent background */
            cursor: pointer;
            outline: none;
            /* Faded out effect */
            opacity: 0.7; 
            /* Smooth transition for hover effects */
            transition: all 0.3s ease-in-out;
        }

        /* Button Styling (Hover State) */
        .waitlist-button:hover {
            background-color: white; /* Full white background */
            color: black; /* Black text */
            opacity: 1; /* Ensure it's fully visible on hover */
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Background Video Element -->
    <!-- !!! IMPORTANT: REPLACE 'your-video-url.mp4' with your actual video file path/URL !!! -->
    <video class="video-background" autoplay loop muted playsinline>
        <source src="your-video-url.mp4" type="video/mp4">
        <!-- Fallback text if video doesn't load -->
        Your browser does not support the video tag.
    </video>

    <!-- Center Content -->
    <div class="hero-content">
        <h1 class="hero-text">Explore Zeroh</h1>

        <button class="waitlist-button">
            Join Waitlist
        </button>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

### 🛠️ How to Use This Code

1.  **Save:** Save the code above as `index.html`.
2.  **Video:** Obtain your video file (e.g., `hero.mp4`). **Crucially, replace** `your-video-url.mp4` in the `<source>` tag with the correct path or URL to your video.
3.  **Test:** Open `index.html` in any modern web browser.
4.  **Functionality Check:**
    *   The background will be the video, contained within a black viewport.
    *   The page will not scroll (`overflow: hidden`).
    *   "Explore Zeroh" will be large, bold, and centered.
    *   The "Join Waitlist" button starts with a transparent background, white outline, and a slightly faded appearance (`opacity: 0.7`).
    *   When you hover over the button, it instantly transitions to a solid white background and black text.

### 💡 Technical Notes

*   **No Scroll:** The CSS rule `overflow: hidden;` on `body, html` prevents any scrolling whatsoever.
*   **Video Setup:** `position: absolute` and `object-fit: cover` ensure the video perfectly covers the entire screen without stretching or leaving empty space.
*   **Centering:** Flexbox (`display: flex`, `justify-content: center`, `align-items: center`) is used on the `.hero-content` to perfectly center all content vertically and horizontally.
*   **Hover:** The `transition: all 0.3s ease-in-out;` property is applied to the button, ensuring the change from transparent/white-outlined to solid white/black text is smooth, not instantaneous.
*   **`muted` and `playsinline`:** These attributes are necessary for the video to autoplay reliably on most mobile devices (iOS/Android).

